      <Comment>|FRAME: N-Acylethanolamines &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acylethanolamines| are a class of endogenous bioactive lipid molecules formed by the linkage of an acyl group to the nitrogen atom of |FRAME: ETHANOL-AMINE|. These compounds exert a variety of biological actions through their interactions with various receptors. One of the &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acylethanolamines, |FRAME: CPD-7598|, has received much attention because it is an endocanabinoid (an endogenous ligand of the cannabinoid receptors CB1 and CB2). The other &lt;i&gt;N&lt;/i&gt;-acylethanolamines do not bind to cannabinoid receptors.</Comment>
